{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall give a life, etc.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory disagree in the Mekhilta: some say it means execution by the court, even though he intended to kill this one and killed that one; and some say it means monetary compensation. And according to the one who says monetary compensation, the verse's use of <b>and you shall give</b> is precise, for it is a matter given hand to hand. And according to the one who says an actual life [for a life], it said <b>and you shall give</b> to teach that in the case of the payment mentioned just above — when there is no loss of life — that is what applies, and there is no other payment there, for he is exempt from damages for the offspring, unless there was loss of life in a manner for which he is not liable, such as where they assessed the blow and determined that it was not lethal — in such a case he is liable, as I have written in connection with the verse (Exodus 21:18): ״וְכִי יְרִיבֻן״."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:01.384257290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}